// About page text: my own words (Nov 19), used exactly. Don't edit without asking.
---
<BaseLayout title="About" drawer="about">
  <article>
    <h1>About Mad Seacow</h1>

    <p>I'm a SaaS sales rep who's becoming a little obsessed with systems, automation, and building things. I like figuring out where the information lives, how to connect the tools that have it, and how to tell when the result is wrong.</p>

    <p>I don't write much code by hand. I design the systems, direct the AI that builds them, and test them against the real thing, whether that's a CRM, a sales team or a picture frame on my wall.</p>

    <p>That's led to a few things I didn't expect to build, including a prospecting pipeline that other reps use, a printable mystery game and a framed <a href="/experiments/living-family-portrait/">e-paper portrait</a> that changes with the weather. Mad Seacow is where I keep track of what I built, what broke, and what I learned.</p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  article {
    max-width: var(--measure);
  }
  h1 {
    margin: 0.25rem 0 1.5rem;
    font-size: clamp(1.9rem, 5vw, 2.6rem);
  }
</style>
